---
/**
 * Shared Parental Pay Calculator UK — 영국판 제도 도구(basis "law"). 한국어판 육아휴직 급여(/guide/parental-leave-pay-calculator/)와
 * 제도가 달라(통상임금 × 지급률 vs 주 정액 £194.32 와 90% 중 낮은 쪽) 짝(hreflang)을 맺지 않는다(조사표 영국 칸 '제도').
 * 계산은 lib/gb/shared-parental-pay.ts(정수 펜스), 화면은 lib/gb/shared-parental-pay-ui.ts, 숫자는 rates/gb/shared-parental-pay-2026.json
 * (GOV.UK Shared Parental Leave and Pay updated_at 2026-10-16 · SSPP (General) Regs 2014 reg 10·32·40 · NI 2015 reg 10·32·40 ·
 * SI 2026/148 art 10(2) — 2026-10-21 확인). birth 부모만(입양·대리모 규정 안 읽음).
 *
 * 소제목은 영국 구글 자동완성에서 왔다(keywords/gb-shared-parental-pay-2026-10-21.csv, hl en · gl gb):
 *   how much is shared parental pay / statutory shared parental pay 2026 · april 2026 · rate · eligibility /
 *   shared parental pay calculator uk · enhanced · for employers / shared parental leave calculator gov.uk
 * 계산하지 않는 것(rates notCalculated): 자격 판정(£129·£390·26주), 입양, SMP 첫 6주, enhanced pay, leave 일정, 과세, 2027-04 이후 금액.
 */
import BaseHead from "../../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import AdSlot from "../../../components/AdSlot.astro";
import ClarityHead from "../../../components/ClarityHead.astro";
import GtagHead from "../../../components/GtagHead.astro";
import TrackLinks from "../../../components/TrackLinks.astro";
import AdSenseHead from "../../../components/AdSenseHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { weeklyRate, nweWeekly, nweMonthly, weeksLeft } from "../../../lib/gb/shared-parental-pay";
import { gbp } from "../../../lib/gb/vat";
import "../../../styles/global.css";

const title = "Shared Parental Pay Calculator UK — ShPP Weekly Rate 2026/27 and Weeks Left";
const description =
  "Work out UK Statutory Shared Parental Pay: £194.32 a week or 90% of average weekly earnings, the daily rate and ShPP weeks left after maternity pay.";

const r300 = weeklyRate(nweWeekly(30000));
const r150 = weeklyRate(nweWeekly(15000));
const r12345 = weeklyRate(nweWeekly(12345));
const cutoff = 21592; // £215.92 — 90% 가 £194.32 를 넘는 첫 금액(그 아래 £215.91 도 올림으로 £194.32)
const m800 = weeklyRate(nweMonthly(160000, 2)!);
const w22 = weeksLeft(22, 0);
const w22p10 = weeksLeft(22, 10);
---

<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
    <ClarityHead />
    <GtagHead />
    <AdSenseHead />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-texture">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <h1>Shared Parental Pay Calculator UK</h1>
      <p>
        Statutory Shared Parental Pay (ShPP) is paid at £194.32 a week or 90% of your average weekly earnings, whichever is lower. Type
        your average weekly earnings to see your weekly and daily ShPP, then work out how many weeks of ShPP are left once maternity pay
        has been taken. This page covers birth parents. It does not check whether you are eligible, and it does not cover adoption or
        surrogacy.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="sp-nwe">Average weekly earnings before tax (£)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="decimal" id="sp-nwe" value="300.00" autocomplete="off" data-ui="off" />
        </div>

        <div class="result-hero" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-dock="sp-value">
          <p class="label">Statutory Shared Parental Pay</p>
          <p class="big" id="sp-value">{gbp(r300.weekly)} a week</p>
          <p class="hint" id="sp-formula">90% of £300.00 is £270.00, so the £194.32 maximum applies</p>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-row">
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Daily rate (one-seventh)</span>
            <span class="value" id="sp-daily">{gbp(r300.daily)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Rule used</span>
            <span class="value" id="sp-rule">£194.32 flat rate</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
          <button id="btn-download" type="button">Save as image</button>
          <button id="btn-share" type="button" class="secondary">Share</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How much is Shared Parental Pay in 2026?</h2>
      <p>
        From 6 April 2026 the weekly rate of ShPP is the smaller of £194.32 and 90% of your normal weekly earnings (regulation 40 of the
        Statutory Shared Parental Pay (General) Regulations 2014). The £194.32 figure was set by the Social Security Benefits Up-rating
        Order 2026; before 6 April 2026 it was £187.18. When the 90% amount, or a daily amount, includes a fraction of a penny, it is
        rounded up to the next penny.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>£300 a week: 90% is £270, which is more than £194.32, so ShPP is {gbp(r300.weekly)} — the example GOV.UK gives</li>
        <li>£150 a week: 90% is {gbp(r150.weekly)}, which is below £194.32, so ShPP is {gbp(r150.weekly)}</li>
        <li>£123.45 a week: 90% is £111.105, rounded up to {gbp(r12345.weekly)}</li>
        <li>From {gbp(cutoff)} a week upwards, 90% is above £194.32, so everyone earning that or more gets the flat {gbp(19432)}</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The rate goes up each April when the government uprates benefits. A rate for April 2027 has not been published, so totals in this
        calculator that run past 5 April 2027 may change.
      </p>

      <h2>Daily rate</h2>
      <p>
        ShPP can be paid for part of a week at a daily rate of one-seventh of the weekly rate. At the flat rate that is £194.32 ÷ 7 =
        {" "}{gbp(r300.daily)} exactly. Below the flat rate, this page takes one-seventh of the 90% figure before it is rounded and rounds
        that up to the penny — for £150 a week, £135 ÷ 7 = £19.285…, so {gbp(r150.daily)}. That is how this page reads regulation 40(2);
        your employer's payroll may differ by a penny.
      </p>

      <h2 id="average-weekly-earnings">How average weekly earnings are worked out</h2>
      <p>
        Your normal weekly earnings are your gross earnings over a "relevant period" of about 8 weeks, ending with the last normal payday
        before the qualifying date (regulation 32). If you are paid monthly, divide the earnings in that period by the number of calendar
        months (rounded to the nearest whole number), multiply by 12 and divide by 52. Otherwise, if the period is not a whole number of
        weeks, divide by the number of days in it and multiply by 7. Your employer works out the exact period from your paydays.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="nw-earn">Gross earnings in the relevant period (£)</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="decimal" id="nw-earn" value="1,600.00" autocomplete="off" data-ui="off" />
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="nw-freq">How are you paid?</label>
          <select id="nw-freq" data-seg>
            <option value="monthly" selected>Monthly</option>
            <option value="days">Weekly or other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label id="nw-count-label" for="nw-count">Calendar months in the period</label>
          <input type="number" id="nw-count" value="2" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric" />
        </div>

        <div class="result-hero" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
          <p class="label">Normal weekly earnings</p>
          <p class="big" id="nw-value">£184.61… a week</p>
          <p class="hint" id="nw-formula">£1,600.00 ÷ 2 × 12 ÷ 52</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Weekly ShPP from this</span>
            <span class="value" id="nw-shpp">{gbp(m800.weekly)}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Earnings of £800 a month for two months work out at £184.61… a week; 90% of that is £166.153…, so ShPP is {gbp(m800.weekly)}. The
        weekly figure itself is not rounded. Copy it into the first calculator if you want the daily rate and totals.
      </p>

      <h2 id="weeks-left">How many weeks of ShPP are left?</h2>
      <p>
        You and your partner can share up to 50 weeks of leave and up to 37 weeks of pay. Under regulation 10, the weeks of ShPP available
        are 39 weeks less the weeks of Statutory Maternity Pay or Maternity Allowance paid to the mother, and less the weeks of ShPP the
        other parent has given notice to claim. Part of a week counts as a whole week. GOV.UK's example: a mother who has taken 22 weeks of
        maternity pay can share {w22.weeks} weeks of ShPP (39 − 22) with her partner.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="wk-smp">Weeks of maternity pay or Maternity Allowance taken</label>
          <input type="number" id="wk-smp" value="22" min="2" max="39" step="1" inputmode="numeric" />
        </div>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="wk-partner">Weeks of ShPP the other parent is claiming</label>
          <input type="number" id="wk-partner" value="0" min="0" max="37" step="1" inputmode="numeric" />
        </div>

        <div class="result-hero" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
          <p class="label">ShPP weeks left for you</p>
          <p class="big" id="wk-value">{w22.weeks} weeks</p>
          <p class="hint" id="wk-formula">39 − 22 − 0 = {w22.weeks}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Total at the weekly rate above</span>
            <span class="value" id="wk-total">{gbp(w22.weeks * r300.weekly)}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label">Worked out as</span>
            <span class="value" id="wk-total-formula">{w22.weeks} × {gbp(r300.weekly)}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        The mother cannot return to work in the first 2 weeks after the birth (4 weeks for factory work), which is why GOV.UK says up to 37
        weeks of pay can be shared. This calculator counts maternity pay as at least 2 weeks. If the other parent claims 10 of the
        {" "}{w22.weeks} weeks, {w22p10.weeks} are left. The total uses today's weekly rate for every week; weeks paid on or after 6 April
        2027 will be at a rate that has not been set yet.
      </p>

      <h2>Northern Ireland</h2>
      <p>
        Northern Ireland has its own Statutory Shared Parental Pay (General) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2015. Regulations 10, 32 and 40
        there give the same 39-week formula, the same way of working out weekly earnings and the same £194.32 or 90% rate with the same
        rounding, so the three calculators above apply there too.
      </p>

      <h2>Statutory Shared Parental Pay eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        This page does not check eligibility. In outline,
        <a href="https://www.gov.uk/shared-parental-leave-and-pay/eligibility-for-birth-parents" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
          >GOV.UK says</a
        > the parent claiming ShPP must have worked for the same employer for at least 26 weeks by the end of the 15th week before the due
        date and earn on average at least £129 a week, and the other parent must also meet work and earnings tests. Use GOV.UK's
        Shared Parental Leave and Pay planning tool to check your own case.
      </p>

      <details>
        <summary>Is enhanced shared parental pay included?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Some employers pay more than the statutory amount under the contract. This calculator only shows statutory ShPP — check your
          employer's policy for anything extra.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does ShPP start at 90% for the first 6 weeks like maternity pay?</summary>
        <p>
          No. GOV.UK says ShPP is the same as Statutory Maternity Pay except that during the first 6 weeks SMP is paid at 90% of whatever
          you earn, with no maximum. ShPP is always the lower of £194.32 and 90%.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I work out leave as well as pay?</summary>
        <p>
          This page counts weeks of pay only. GOV.UK's example says a mother who has taken 22 weeks of maternity leave can share 30 weeks of
          Shared Parental Leave, and leave must be booked with at least 8 weeks' notice.
        </p>
      </details>

      <p>
        Related: <a href="/en-gb/holiday-entitlement/">holiday entitlement calculator</a> and the
        <a href="/en-gb/tools/date-diff/">date calculator</a> for counting weeks between dates.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.gov.uk/shared-parental-leave-and-pay" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GOV.UK — Shared Parental Leave and Pay</a>
          (updated 16 October 2026, checked 21 October 2026)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2014/3051/contents" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
            >The Statutory Shared Parental Pay (General) Regulations 2014</a
          >, regulations 10, 32 and 40 (checked 21 October 2026)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2026/148/article/10/made" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
            >The Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026</a
          >, article 10 (checked 21 October 2026)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisr/2015/94/contents" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
            >The Statutory Shared Parental Pay (General) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2015</a
          >, regulations 10, 32 and 40 (checked 21 October 2026)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <AdSlot label="shpp-result-en-gb" />
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
    <script src="../../../lib/gb/shared-parental-pay-ui.ts"></script>
    <TrackLinks />
    <script src="../../../scripts/calc-ui.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
